            "providerContent": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Alberto's Fraud Detection Agent is built for an online event ticketing platform. It reviews newly published events and organizers, then gives a human admin an approve, reject, or request-info recommendation along with the reasons.\n\nIt uses graded autonomy: it auto-approves only when the evidence is verified in code, and web sources can hold a decision back but can never approve one.\n\nThe project is currently in offline evals, on 31 test cases:\n- With a local 9B model, approved fraud fell from 54% to 8% over twelve iterations, and fraud approved without a human fell from 27% to 0%.\n- For deployment, Alberto chose Claude Haiku 4.5 (the tool result says \"Claude Haiku 5.5\", so please check that name with him). It reached 86% accuracy vs 71% for the local model, and approved 1% of fraud vs 8%. It costs about $0.002 per review.\n- Haiku escalates more cases to a human, which is the trade-off behind the higher accuracy.\n\nThe stack is TypeScript, PostgreSQL and GCP."
              }
            ]
